The clans of Edom were: clans Timna, Aliah, Jetheth,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 1, 52, 'Oholibamah, Elah, Pinon,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 1, 53, 'Kenaz, Teman, Mibzar,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 1, 54, 'Magdiel, and Iram; these are the clans of Edom.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

The sons of Hur the firstborn of Ephrathah: Shobal father of Kiriath-jearim,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 2, 51, 'Salma father of Bethlehem, and Hareph father of Beth-gader.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 2, 52, 'Shobal father of Kiriath-jearim had other sons: Haroeh, half of the Menuhoth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 2, 53, 'And the families of Kiriath-jearim: the Ithrites, the Puthites, the Shumathites, and the Mishraites; from these came the Zorathites and the Eshtaolites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 2, 54, 'The sons of Salma: Bethlehem, the Netophathites, Atroth-beth-joab, and half of the Manahathites, the Zorites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 2, 55, 'The families also of the scribes that lived at Jabez: the Tirathites, the Shimeathites, and the Sucathites. These are the Kenites who came from Hammath, father of the house of Rechab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);










"We are yours, O David;  
    and with you, O son of Jesse!  
Peace, peace to you,  
    and peace to the one who helps you!  
    For your God is the one who helps you."
Then David received them, and made them officers of his troops.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 19, 'Some of the Manassites deserted to David when he came with the Philistines for the battle against Saul. (Yet he did not help them, for the rulers of the Philistines took counsel and sent him away, saying, "He will desert to his master Saul at the cost of our heads.")', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 20, 'As he went to Ziklag these Manassites deserted to him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, chiefs of the thousands in Manasseh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 21, 'They helped David against the band of raiders, for they were all warriors and commanders in the army.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 22, 'Indeed from day to day people kept coming to David to help him, until there was a great army, like an army of God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 23, 'These are the numbers of the divisions of the armed troops who came to David in Hebron to turn the kingdom of Saul over to him, according to the word of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David"s Army at Hebron'),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 24, 'The people of Judah bearing shield and spear numbered six thousand eight hundred armed troops.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 25, 'Of the Simeonites, mighty warriors, seven thousand one hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 26, 'Of the Levites four thousand six hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 27, 'Jehoiada, leader of the house of Aaron, and with him three thousand seven hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 28, 'Zadok, a young warrior, and twenty-two commanders from his own ancestral house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 29, 'Of the Benjaminites, the kindred of Saul, three thousand, of whom the majority had continued to keep their allegiance to the house of Saul.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 30, 'Of the Ephraimites, twenty thousand eight hundred, mighty warriors, notables in their ancestral houses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 31, 'Of the half-tribe of Manasseh, eighteen thousand, who were expressly named to come and make David king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 32, 'Of Issachar, those who had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do, two hundred chiefs, and all their kindred under their command.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 33, 'Of Zebulun, fifty thousand seasoned troops, equipped for battle with all the weapons of war, to help David with singleness of purpose.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 34, 'Of Naphtali, a thousand commanders, with whom there were thirty-seven thousand armed with shield and spear.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 35, 'Of the Danites, twenty-eight thousand six hundred equipped for battle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 36, 'Of Asher, forty thousand seasoned troops ready for battle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 37, 'Of the Reubenites and Gadites and the half-tribe of Manasseh from beyond the Jordan, one hundred twenty thousand armed with all the weapons of war.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 38, 'All these, warriors arrayed in battle order, came to Hebron with full intent to make David king over all Israel; likewise all the rest of Israel were of a single mind to make David king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 39, 'They were there with David for three days, eating and drinking, for their kindred had provided for them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 12, 40, 'And also their neighbors, from as far away as Issachar and Zebulun and Naphtali, came bringing food on donkeys, camels, mules, and oxen--abundant provisions of meal, cakes of figs, clusters of raisins, wine, oil, oxen, and sheep, for there was joy in Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);




    make known his deeds among the peoples.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 9, 'Sing to him, sing praises to him,  
    tell of all his wonderful works.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 10, 'Glory in his holy name;  
    let the hearts of those who seek the LORD rejoice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 11, 'Seek the LORD and his strength,  
    seek his presence continually.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 12, 'Remember the wonderful works he has done,  
    his miracles, and the judgments he uttered,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 13, 'O offspring of his servant Israel,  
    children of Jacob, his chosen ones.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 14, 'He is the LORD our God;  
    his judgments are in all the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 15, 'Remember his covenant forever,  
    the word that he commanded, for a thousand generations,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 16, 'the covenant that he made with Abraham,  
    his sworn promise to Isaac,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 17, 'which he confirmed to Jacob as a statute,  
    to Israel as an everlasting covenant,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 18, 'saying, "To you I will give the land of Canaan  
    as your portion for an inheritance."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 19, 'When they were few in number,  
    of little account, and strangers in the land,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 20, 'wandering from nation to nation,  
    from one kingdom to another people,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 21, 'he allowed no one to oppress them;  
    he rebuked kings on their account,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 22, 'saying, "Do not touch my anointed ones;  
    do my prophets no harm."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 23, 'Sing to the LORD, all the earth.  
    Tell of his salvation from day to day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 24, 'Declare his glory among the nations,  
    his marvelous works among all the peoples.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 25, 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised;  
    he is to be revered above all gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 26, 'For all the gods of the peoples are idols,  
    but the LORD made the heavens.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 27, 'Honor and majesty are before him;  
    strength and joy are in his place.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 28, 'Ascribe to the LORD, O families of the peoples,  
    ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 29, 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due his name;  
    bring an offering, and come before him.  
Worship the LORD in holy splendor;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 30, 'tremble before him, all the earth.  
    The world is firmly established; it shall never be moved.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 31, 'Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice,  
    and let them say among the nations, "The LORD is king!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 32, 'Let the sea roar, and all that fills it;  
    let the field exult, and everything in it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 33, 'Then shall the trees of the forest sing for joy  
    before the LORD, for he comes to judge the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 34, 'O give thanks to the LORD, for he is good;  
    for his steadfast love endures forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 35, 'Say also:
"Save us, O God of our salvation,  
    and gather and rescue us from among the nations,  
that we may give thanks to your holy name,  
    and glory in your praise.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 36, 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,  
    from everlasting to everlasting."
Then all the people said "Amen!" and praised the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 37, 'David left Asaph and his kinsfolk there before the ark of the covenant of the LORD to minister regularly before the ark as each day required,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Regular Worship Maintained'),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 38, 'and also Obed-edom and his sixty-eight kinsfolk; while Obed-edom son of Jeduthun and Hosah were to be gatekeepers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 39, 'And he left the priest Zadok and his kindred the priests before the tabernacle of the LORD in the high place that was at Gibeon,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 40, 'to offer burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offering regularly, morning and evening, according to all that is written in the law of the LORD that he commanded Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 41, 'With them were Heman and Jeduthun, and the rest of those chosen and expressly named to render thanks to the LORD, for his steadfast love endures forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 42, 'Heman and Jeduthun had with them trumpets and cymbals for the music, and instruments for sacred song. The sons of Jeduthun were appointed to the gate.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 16, 43, 'Then all the people departed to their homes, and David went home to bless his household.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

Moreover I declare to you that the LORD will build you a house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 11, 'When your days are fulfilled to go to be with your ancestors, I will raise up your offspring after you, one of your own sons, and I will establish his kingdom.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 12, 'He shall build a house for me, and I will establish his throne forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 13, 'I will be a father to him, and he shall be a son to me. I will not take my steadfast love from him, as I took it from him who was before you,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 14, 'but I will confirm him in my house and in my kingdom forever, and his throne shall be established forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 15, 'In accordance with all these words and all this vision, Nathan spoke to David.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 16, 'Then King David went in and sat before the LORD, and said, "Who am I, O LORD God, and what is my house, that you have brought me thus far?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David"s Prayer'),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 17, 'And even this was a small thing in your sight, O God; you have also spoken of your servant"s house for a great while to come. You regard me as someone of high rank, O LORD God!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 18, 'And what more can David say to you for honoring your servant? You know your servant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 19, 'For your servant"s sake, O LORD, and according to your own heart, you have done all these great deeds, making known all these great things.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 20, 'There is no one like you, O LORD, and there is no God besides you, according to all that we have heard with our ears.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 21, 'Who is like your people Israel, one nation on the earth whom God went to redeem to be his people, making for yourself a name for great and terrible things, in driving out nations before your people whom you redeemed from Egypt?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 22, 'And you made your people Israel to be your people forever; and you, O LORD, became their God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 23, '"And now, O LORD, as for the word that you have spoken concerning your servant and concerning his house, let it be established forever, and do as you have promised.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 24, 'Thus your name will be established and magnified forever in the saying, "The LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, is Israel"s God"; and the house of your servant David will be established in your presence.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 25, 'For you, my God, have revealed to your servant that you will build a house for him; therefore your servant has found it possible to pray before you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 26, 'And now, O LORD, you are God, and you have promised this good thing to your servant;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 17, 27, 'therefore may it please you to bless the house of your servant, that it may continue forever before you. For you, O LORD, have blessed and are blessed forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);












They made David"s son Solomon king a second time; they anointed him as the LORD"s prince, and Zadok as priest.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Solomon Anointed King'),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 23, 'Then Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD, succeeding his father David as king; he prospered, and all Israel obeyed him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 24, 'All the leaders and the mighty warriors, and also all the sons of King David, pledged their allegiance to King Solomon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 25, 'The LORD highly exalted Solomon in the sight of all Israel, and bestowed upon him such royal majesty as had not been on any king before him in Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 26, 'Thus David son of Jesse reigned over all Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Summary of David"s Reign'),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 27, 'The period that he reigned over Israel was forty years; he reigned seven years in Hebron, and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 28, 'He died in a good old age, full of days, riches, and honor; and his son Solomon succeeded him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 29, 'Now the acts of King David, from first to last, are written in the records of the seer Samuel, and in the records of the prophet Nathan, and in the records of the seer Gad,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(13, '1 Taw', '1 Chronicles', 29, 30, 'with accounts of all his rule and his might and of the events that befell him and Israel and all the kingdoms of the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);





"For he is good,  
    for his steadfast love endures forever,"
the house, the house of the LORD, was filled with a cloud,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 5, 14, 'so that the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud; for the glory of the LORD filled the house of God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

    you and the ark of your might.  
Let your priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation,  
    and let your faithful rejoice in your goodness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 6, 42, 'O LORD God, do not reject your anointed one.  
    Remember your steadfast love for your servant David."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"For he is good,  
    for his steadfast love endures forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 4, 'Then the king and all the people offered sacrifice before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 5, 'King Solomon offered as a sacrifice twenty-two thousand oxen and one hundred twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the people dedicated the house of God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 6, 'The priests stood at their posts; the Levites also, with the instruments for music to the LORD that King David had made for giving thanks to the LORD--for his steadfast love endures forever--whenever David offered praises by their ministry. Opposite them the priests sounded trumpets; and all Israel stood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 7, 'Solomon consecrated the middle of the court that was in front of the house of the LORD; for there he offered the burnt offerings and the fat of the offerings of well-being because the bronze altar Solomon had made could not hold the burnt offering and the grain offering and the fat parts.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 8, 'At that time Solomon held the festival for seven days, and all Israel with him, a very great congregation, from Lebo-hamath to the Wadi of Egypt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 9, 'On the eighth day they held a solemn assembly; for they had observed the dedication of the altar seven days and the festival seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 10, 'On the twenty-third day of the seventh month he sent the people away to their homes, joyful and in good spirits because of the goodness that the LORD had shown to David and to Solomon and to his people Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 11, 'Thus Solomon finished the house of the LORD and the king"s house; all that Solomon had planned to do in the house of the LORD and in his own house he successfully accomplished.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 12, 'Then the LORD appeared to Solomon in the night and said to him: "I have heard your prayer, and have chosen this place for myself as a house of sacrifice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'God"s Second Appearance to Solomon'),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 13, 'When I shut up the heavens so that there is no rain, or command the locust to devour the land, or send pestilence among my people,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 14, 'if my people who are called by my name humble themselves, pray, seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways, then I will hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin and heal their land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 15, 'Now my eyes will be open and my ears attentive to the prayer that is made in this place.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 16, 'For now I have chosen and consecrated this house so that my name may be there forever; my eyes and my heart will be there for all time.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 17, 'As for you, if you walk before me, as your father David walked, doing according to all that I have commanded you and keeping my statutes and my ordinances,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 18, 'then I will establish your royal throne, as I made covenant with your father David saying, "You shall never lack a successor to rule over Israel."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 19, '"But if you turn aside and forsake my statutes and my commandments that I have set before you, and go and serve other gods and worship them,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 20, 'then I will pluck you up from the land that I have given you; and this house, which I have consecrated for my name, I will cast out of my sight, and will make it a proverb and a byword among all peoples.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 21, 'And regarding this house, now exalted, everyone passing by will be astonished, and say, "Why has the LORD done such a thing to this land and to this house?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 7, 22, 'Then they will say, "Because they abandoned the LORD the God of their ancestors who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and they adopted other gods, and worshiped them and served them; therefore he has brought all this calamity upon them.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



"What share do we have in David?  
    We have no inheritance in the son of Jesse.  
Each of you to your tents, O Israel!  
    Look now to your own house, O David."
So all Israel departed to their tents.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 10, 17, 'But Rehoboam reigned over the people of Israel who were living in the cities of Judah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 10, 18, 'When King Rehoboam sent Hadoram, who was taskmaster over the forced labor, the people of Israel stoned him to death. King Rehoboam hurriedly mounted his chariot to flee to Jerusalem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 10, 19, 'So Israel has been in rebellion against the house of David to this day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



Now there was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 3, 'Abijah engaged in battle, having an army of valiant warriors, four hundred thousand picked men; and Jeroboam drew up his line of battle against him with eight hundred thousand picked mighty warriors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 4, 'Then Abijah stood on the slope of Mount Zemaraim that is in the hill country of Ephraim, and said, "Listen to me, Jeroboam and all Israel!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 5, 'Do you not know that the LORD God of Israel gave the kingship over Israel forever to David and his sons by a covenant of salt?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 6, 'Yet Jeroboam son of Nebat, a servant of Solomon son of David, rose up and rebelled against his lord;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 7, 'and certain worthless scoundrels gathered around him and defied Rehoboam son of Solomon, when Rehoboam was young and irresolute and could not withstand them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 8, '"And now you think that you can withstand the kingdom of the LORD in the hand of the sons of David, because you are a great multitude and have with you the golden calves that Jeroboam made as gods for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 9, 'Have you not driven out the priests of the LORD, the descendants of Aaron, and the Levites, and made priests for yourselves like the peoples of other lands? Whoever comes to be consecrated with a young bull or seven rams becomes a priest of what are no gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 10, 'But as for us, the LORD is our God, and we have not abandoned him. We have priests ministering to the LORD who are descendants of Aaron, and Levites for their service.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 11, 'They offer to the LORD every morning and every evening burnt offerings and fragrant incense, set out the rows of bread on the table of pure gold, and care for the golden lampstand so that its lamps may burn every evening; for we keep the charge of the LORD our God, but you have abandoned him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 12, 'See, God is with us at our head, and his priests have their battle trumpets to sound the call to battle against you. O Israelites, do not fight against the LORD, the God of your ancestors; for you cannot succeed."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 13, 'Jeroboam had sent an ambush around to come on them from behind; thus his troops were in front of Judah, and the ambush was behind them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 14, 'When Judah turned, the battle was in front of them and behind them. They cried out to the LORD, and the priests blew the trumpets.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 15, 'Then the people of Judah raised the battle shout. And when the people of Judah shouted, God defeated Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 16, 'The Israelites fled before Judah, and God gave them into their hands.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 17, 'Abijah and his army defeated them with great slaughter; five hundred thousand picked men of Israel fell slain.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 18, 'Thus the Israelites were subdued at that time, and the people of Judah prevailed, because they relied on the LORD, the God of their ancestors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 19, 'Abijah pursued Jeroboam, and took cities from him: Bethel with its villages and Jeshanah with its villages and Ephron with its villages.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 20, 'Jeroboam did not recover his power in the days of Abijah; the LORD struck him down, and he died.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 21, 'But Abijah grew strong. He took fourteen wives, and became the father of twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 13, 22, 'The rest of the acts of Abijah, his behavior and his deeds, are written in the story of the prophet Iddo.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







"Give thanks to the LORD,  
    for his steadfast love endures forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 22, 'As they began to sing and praise, the LORD set an ambush against the Ammonites, Moab, and Mount Seir, who had come against Judah, so that they were routed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 23, 'For the Ammonites and Moab attacked the inhabitants of Mount Seir, destroying them utterly; and when they had made an end of the inhabitants of Seir, they all helped to destroy one another.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 24, 'When Judah came to the watchtower of the wilderness, they looked toward the multitude; they were corpses lying on the ground; no one had escaped.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 25, 'When Jehoshaphat and his people came to take the booty from them, they found livestock in great numbers, goods, clothing, and precious things, which they took for themselves until they could carry no more. They spent three days taking the booty, because of its abundance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 26, 'On the fourth day they assembled in the Valley of Beracah, for there they blessed the LORD; therefore that place has been called the Valley of Beracah to this day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 27, 'Then all the people of Judah and Jerusalem, with Jehoshaphat at their head, returned to Jerusalem with joy, for the LORD had enabled them to rejoice over their enemies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 28, 'They came to Jerusalem, with harps and lyres and trumpets, to the house of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 29, 'The fear of God came on all the kingdoms of the countries when they heard that the LORD had fought against the enemies of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 30, 'And the realm of Jehoshaphat was quiet, for his God gave him rest all around.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 31, 'So Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah. He was thirty-five years old when he began to reign; he reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother"s name was Azubah daughter of Shilhi.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The End of Jehoshaphat"s Reign'),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 32, 'He walked in the way of his father Asa and did not turn aside from it, doing what was right in the sight of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 33, 'Yet the high places were not removed; the people had not yet set their hearts upon the God of their ancestors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 34, 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, from first to last, are written in the Annals of Jehu son of Hanani, which are recorded in the Book of the Kings of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 35, 'After this King Jehoshaphat of Judah joined with King Ahaziah of Israel, who did wickedly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 36, 'He joined him in building ships to go to Tarshish; they built the ships in Ezion-geber.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(14, '2 Taw', '2 Chronicles', 20, 37, 'Then Eliezer son of Dodavahu of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, "Because you have joined with Ahaziah, the LORD will destroy what you have made." And the ships were wrecked and were not able to go to Tarshish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

















